 ## Background
-Boolean Voxel Meshing is one of the earliest and simplest methods for converting voxel data to polygonal meshes, often associated with the aesthetic of games like Minecraft [S1, S4, unofficial]. It was popularized in early voxel engine tutorials and implementations, such as those described in Stack Overflow discussions on VBO generation for voxel chunks [S1, unofficial]. The method is used in various open-source projects for OBJ export [S3, unofficial] and WebGL mesh generation [S7, unofficial]. Variants like MicroBlockBuilder extend this concept to allow complex shapes (stairs, slabs) by subdividing voxels into smaller boolean arrays [S5, unofficial].
